From: Julian Decker <git@deckerjulian.com>
Subject: drm/rockchip: logo: do not read modes for a route without a clock

setup_initial_state() fills the connector's mode list to find the mode the
boot loader used. A mode only matches when its pixel clock equals the one
from the boot loader, so when that clock is zero the outcome is known
before the list exists, but the sink is read all the same. For HDMI that is
an EDID read, which takes up to a second on some sinks.

Skip get_modes() in that case. rockchip_drm_fill_connector_modes() still
runs up to that point, so detection, its hot-plug event and the polling set
up there stay as they were. The connector is then reported as disconnected
and the route takes the existing way of a route with nothing connected:
no modes, loader_protect undone, and the CRTC closed from the unset list.

A route with force-output is left alone, as forcing the connector and
adding the fallback modes happens in the same function.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c
@@ -595,7 +595,7 @@
 
 static int rockchip_drm_fill_connector_modes(struct drm_connector *connector,
 					     uint32_t maxX, uint32_t maxY,
-					     bool force_output)
+					     bool force_output, bool skip_modes)
 {
 	struct drm_device *dev = connector->dev;
 	struct drm_display_mode *mode;
@@ -669,6 +669,11 @@
 		goto prune;
 	}
 
+	if (skip_modes) {
+		connector->status = connector_status_disconnected;
+		goto prune;
+	}
+
 	count = (*connector_funcs->get_modes)(connector);
 
 	if (count == 0 && connector->status == connector_status_connected)
@@ -840,7 +845,13 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	num_modes = rockchip_drm_fill_connector_modes(connector, 7680, 7680, set->force_output);
+	/*
+	 * Without a pixel clock from the boot loader no mode can match, so
+	 * reading the display's modes (for HDMI, its EDID) would only cost
+	 * time. The route then goes the way of one with nothing connected.
+	 */
+	num_modes = rockchip_drm_fill_connector_modes(connector, 7680, 7680, set->force_output,
+						      !set->clock && !set->force_output);
 	if (!num_modes) {
 		dev_err(drm_dev->dev, "connector[%s] can't find any modes\n",
 			connector->name);
